==Rules==
{{StageRule|13thAnni}}

==Battleground==
*3 [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*2 [[Madam Peng]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Malizabeth]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Grand Emperor Warumongar]] spawns as the boss.
**20 [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**3 [[Malizabeth]]s spawn, delay 106.67~110 seconds<sup>3,200f~3,300f</sup>.
**1 [[Enchanting Mage Vibon]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
**1 [[St. Dober]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
**3 [[Madam Peng]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 86.67~90 seconds<sup>2,600f~2,700f</sup>.
**1 [[Capy]] spawns after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You don't wanna waste any cash here. Stack up [[Scarf Cat (Special Cat)|Red Nyanko Rangers]], [[Commander Cat (Special Cat)|Gold Nyanko Rangers]], and [[Barista Cat (Special Cat)|Silver Nyanko Rangers]] on the Kaijin at the start, then gun it straight for the enemy base.

[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] in tandem hold off the bosses well. Really, the bulk of your lineup should be dedicated to countering God's strongest pain in the neck: St. Dober. [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cats]], [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cats]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cats]], Silver Nyanko Rangers, you name it, it should all be put to bursting down Dober. You can optionally time a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]/[[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt Cannon]] to hopefully get a few hits in on Dober as well, though this is beyond inconsistent due to the constant stream of Surge Attacks and Explosions from every which way. Capy is a non-issue for the most part, and only necessitates that you bring [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] as a hard-counter.

Leaving the main peons in the dust means you can focus on chipping down Grand Emperor Warumongar, as he is immune to Gold Nyanko Ranger's Knockback, and is extremely difficult to make budge. Red Nyanko Ranger and Can Can Cat are best suited for this job, especially if you've boosted them. [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] is highly recommended to make cleanup much less stressful, since you will start running low on funds as war draws to its end. When Warumongar dies, it means the end of all evil. They have no more tricks, nor traps left; it's tit for tat, so get it over with.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Helps in stopping St. Dober's advance and holds Vibon still if need be. He can even be useful against Capy, if he survives long enough, that is.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Difficult to get a direct hit on anything with all of the Surges, but good timing is rewarded in spades. You can also use Malizabeths and Madam Pengs as stepping to snipe incoming enemies and even the bosses.

